.TH SLATE 1 "October 2026" "Slate" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
slate, slate-gui \- shared terminal and graphical text editor
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B slate
[OPTIONS] [+LINE[,COLUMN]] [FILE...]
.br
.B slate-gui
[OPTIONS] [FILE...|DIRECTORY]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Slate uses one Rust editing core for its terminal and Qt Quick interfaces.
A directory opens a rooted workspace. Standard input is accepted as a file
argument of a single dash. Missing files are created when saved.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --tui, --gui
Choose the interface.
.TP
.B -v, --view
Open files read-only.
.TP
.B --fresh
Skip restoring the prior recovery checkpoint.
.TP
.B --editor-only, --workspace
Choose the initial layout.
.TP
.B --new-instance
Open a separate graphical window.
.TP
.B -B, --backup
Keep the previous saved file as NAME~.
.TP
.B -S, --softwrap
Wrap long lines on screen.
.TP
.B -l, --linenumbers
Display line numbers.
.TP
.B -E, --tabstospaces
Insert spaces for typed tabs.
.TP
.B -T N, --tabsize=N
Set tab display width to 1\(en32 columns.
.TP
.B -H, --historylog
Persist search and replacement history (up to 100 entries each).
.TP
.B -G, --locking
Warn about files open in another Slate instance or with another editor's swap file.
Editing remains allowed; locks are advisory.
.TP
.B -I, --ignorercfiles
Use default Slate preferences for this session. EditorConfig still applies.
.TP
.B -i, --autoindent
Automatically indent new lines.
.TP
.B -m, --mouse
Enable terminal mouse support.
.TP
.B -h, --help
Show command help.
.TP
.B -V, --version
Show the version.
.SH KEYS
F1 or Ctrl-Shift-P opens the command palette. Ctrl-S saves, Ctrl-F finds,
Ctrl-H replaces, Ctrl-Q quits. Choose keymap = "nano" in settings for nano
bindings. Find/replace accepts Alt-R for regex, Alt-S for selection scope,
and Up/Down for history. Alt-Shift-drag selects a rectangle.
.SH FILES
Configuration is under $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/slate (normally ~/.config/slate).
Recovery, history and diagnostics are under $XDG_STATE_HOME/slate
(normally ~/.local/state/slate). Preferences and profiles use TOML.
.SH SEE ALSO
The repository README, docs/SUPPORT.md, and the shared command palette.
